target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestTheDecodeErrorNamesWhatTheOperatorMustGoFix'
expect: must be capped, not copied
why:    the phase is writer-supplied like run_id and the gate names, and it is interpolated into the operator message. Measured before the cap: a 1 MiB phase produced a 4 MiB message, and twenty such rows produced 80 MiB. The gate-name caps did not bound this site — the third instance of the same omission in this one function's neighbourhood.
--- old
	shown := phase
	if len(shown) > maxGateNameLen {
		shown = shown[:maxGateNameLen] + "..."
	}
--- new
	shown := phase
